.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ERR_ERROR_STRING 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ERR_error_string ,
.Nm ERR_error_string_n ,
.Nm ERR_lib_error_string ,
.Nm ERR_func_error_string ,
.Nm ERR_reason_error_string
.Nd obtain human-readable error message
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/err.h
.Ft char *
.Fo ERR_error_string
.Fa "unsigned long e"
.Fa "char *buf"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_error_string_n
.Fa "unsigned long e"
.Fa "char *buf"
.Fa "size_t len"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo ERR_lib_error_string
.Fa "unsigned long e"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo ERR_reason_error_string
.Fa "unsigned long e"
.Fc
Deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0:
.Ft const char *
.Fo ERR_func_error_string
.Fa "unsigned long e"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ERR_error_string
generates a human-readable string representing the error code
.Fa e ,
and places it at
.Fa buf .
.Fa buf
must be at least 256 bytes long.
If
.Fa buf
is
.Dv NULL ,
the error string is placed in a static buffer.
Note that this function is not thread-safe and does no checks on the
size of the buffer; use
.Fn ERR_error_string_n
instead.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_error_string_n
is a variant of
.Fn ERR_error_string
that writes at most
.Fa len
characters (including the terminating 0) and truncates the string if
necessary.
For
.Fn ERR_error_string_n ,
.Fa buf
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Pp
The string will have the following format:
.Bd -literal
 error:[error code]:[library name]::[reason string]
.Ed
.Pp
.Em error code
is an 8 digit hexadecimal number,
.Em library name
and
.Em reason string
are ASCII text.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_lib_error_string
and
.Fn ERR_reason_error_string
return the library name and reason string respectively.
.Pp
If there is no text string registered for the given error code, the
error string will contain the numeric code.
.Pp
.Xr ERR_print_errors 3
can be used to print all error codes currently in the queue.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ERR_error_string
returns a pointer to a static buffer containing the string if
.Fa buf
.Sy == NULL ,
.Fa buf
otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_lib_error_string
and
.Fn ERR_reason_error_string
return the strings, and
.Dv NULL
if none is registered for the error code.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_func_error_string
returns NULL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr ERR_print_errors 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn ERR_func_error_string
became deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
